\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  In the Name of Jesus
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Every knee shall bow,
\par Every tongue confess Him
\par King of Glory now;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 'Tis the Father's pleasure
\par We should call Him Lord,
\par Who from the beginning
\par Was the mighty Word.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Humbled for a season,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 To receive a name
\par From the lips of sinners,
\par Unto whom He came,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Faithfully He bore it
\par Spotless to the last;
\par Brought it back victorious,
\par When from death He passed.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Name Him, brothers, name Him
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 With love strong as death,
\par But with awe and wonder
\par And with bated breath!
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par He is God the Saviour,
\par He is Christ the Lord,
\par Ever to be worshipped,
\par Trusted, and adored.
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  In your hearts enthrone Him;
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 There let Him subdue
\par All that is not holy,
\par All that is not true:
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Crown Him as your Captain
\par In temptation's hour;
\par Let His will enfold you
\par In its light and power.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Brothers, this Lord Jesus
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Shall return again,
\par With His Father's glory,
\par With His angel train;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par For all wreaths of empire
\par Meet upon His brow,
\par And our hearts confess Him
\par King of Glory now.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

